{title: Tell Me the Stories of Jesus}
{artist: William H. Parker / Frederic A. Challinor}
{genre: Children}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: C}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Baptist Hymnal, edited by Walter Hines Sims (Nashville, Tennessee: Convention Press, 1956), # 505)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Tell me the stories of Jesus
[G7]I love to [C]hear;
[C]Things I would ask Him to tell me
[D7]If He were [G7]here;
[G7]Scenes by the [Am]way[C7]side,
[C7]Tales of the [A7]sea,__[Dm]__
[G7]Stories of [Am]Jesus, [G7]tell them to [C]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]First let me hear how the children
[G7]Stood round His [C]knee,
[C]And I shall fancy His blessing
[D7]Resting on [G7]me;
[G7]Words full of [Am]kind[C7]ness,
[C7]Deeds full of [A7]grace,__[Dm]__
[G7]All in the [Am]love light [G7]of Jesus’ [C]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Tell me, in accents of wonder,
[G7]How rolled the [C]sea,
[C]Tossing the boat in a tempest
[D7]On Gali[G7]lee;
[G7]And how the [Am]Mak[C7]er,
[C7]Ready and [A7]kind,__[Dm]__
[G7]Chided the [Am]billows,
[G7]And hushed the [C]wind.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Into the city I’d follow
[G7]The children’s [C]band,
[C]Waving a branch of the palm tree
[D7]High in my [G7]hand.
[G7]One of His [Am]her[C7]alds,
[C7]Yes, I would [A7]sing__[Dm]__
[G7]Loudest ho[Am]sannas,
[G7]Jesus is [C]King!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]Tell how the sparrow that twitters
[G7]On yonder [C]tree,
[C]And the sweet meadow-side lily
[D7]May speak to [G7]me—
[G7]Give me their [Am]mes[C7]sage,
[C7]For I would [A7]hear__[Dm]__
[G7]How Jesus [Am]taught us
[G7]Our Father’s [C]care.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[C]Show me that scene in the garden,
[G7]Of bitter [C]pain.
[C]Show me the cross where my Savior
[D7]For me was [G7]slain.
[G7]Sad ones or [Am]bright [C7]ones,
[C7]So that they [A7]be__[Dm]__
[G7]Stories of [Am]Jesus,
[G7]Tell them to [C]me.
{end_of_verse}
